WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:04.480
- [Mark] Okay, so Matthew, where ya from?

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.313
- West Virginia.

00:00:06.476 --> 00:00:07.666
- [Mark] What part of West Virginia,

00:00:07.666 --> 00:00:08.810
Appalachian part of West Virginia?

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.997
- [Matt] Yes, Princeton.

00:00:09.997 --> 00:00:13.377
- [Mark] Princeton, so that's
the farthest west part.

00:00:13.377 --> 00:00:14.630
- [Matt] Yes.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.880
Right beside of Virginia.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.500
- [Mark] Yeah, no, it's a
beautiful part of the country.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.875
- Oh, it's beautiful.

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:21.311
- [Mark] You miss it?

00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:22.986
- I miss it a lot.

00:00:22.986 --> 00:00:24.301
- [Mark] Can I ask you to
speak a little bit louder

00:00:24.301 --> 00:00:25.506
so I can (indistinct).

00:00:25.506 --> 00:00:26.420
- I miss it a lot.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.935
- [Mark] Yeah, no, it's an
amazing part of the world.

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:29.935
- Yes it is.

00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:33.580
- [Mark] And what brought
you out to California?

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.020
- I was in Arizona and couldn't get ID.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.853
- [Mark] Couldn't get what?

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:37.711
- ID.

00:00:37.711 --> 00:00:38.700
- [Mark] Oh, you couldn't get an ID?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.603
- Yeah, somebody, 27 years ago in Arizona,

00:00:41.603 --> 00:00:43.110
got ahold of my birth certificate

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.255
and obtained an Arizona driver's license.

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:48.740
But they don't have no record
of who they gave it to.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:49.950
I don't see how that's possible.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.620
You don't just hand out driver's license

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.793
with no picture, right?

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.408
So they wouldn't give
me ID, but I've had a ID

00:00:56.408 --> 00:00:58.861
everywhere else, though.

00:00:58.861 --> 00:00:59.694
- [Mark] How?

00:00:59.694 --> 00:01:02.720
- I've had ID in Arizona,
Oklahoma, Kansas,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.560
Florida, New Mexico,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.580
everywhere I've been at,

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.210
West Virginia I had ID,
Virginia, Pennsylvania,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.423
it's just Arizona who's messing me over.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.273
- [Mark] All right.

00:01:15.273 --> 00:01:17.976
- But I came out here and
got my ID with no problems.

00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:19.093
- [Mark] Okay.

00:01:19.093 --> 00:01:19.965
What was your line of work?

00:01:19.965 --> 00:01:21.000
What were you doing for a living?

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.380
- I did restaurant work.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.213
- [Mark] Okay.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.370
And how old are you?

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.192
- I'm 51 years old.

00:01:28.192 --> 00:01:29.775
- [Mark] Fifty-one.

00:01:31.584 --> 00:01:33.310
Now you're down here on Skid Row.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.350
How'd you end up down here?

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.243
- That's the only place to
go when you're homeless.

00:01:38.243 --> 00:01:39.076
- [Mark] Hm.

00:01:39.076 --> 00:01:40.037
- That's where all the shelters are at.

00:01:40.037 --> 00:01:40.870
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:41.703
- [Mark] You can get fed here, and-

00:01:41.703 --> 00:01:43.543
- You can get fed here, get housing here,

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:45.850
yeah, medical.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.700
- [Mark] Yeah.
- Yeah, so.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.230
- [Mark] That's pretty rough
on the streets, though.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.063
- Oh yeah.

00:01:51.063 --> 00:01:53.853
I've seen people hurt here really bad.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.553
- [Mark] Like what have you seen?

00:01:55.553 --> 00:01:57.693
- I've seen a girl get her throat cut.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.750
I've seen another guy
get beat with a chair.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.143
One of them metal chairs
like you see on WWF shit?

00:02:05.143 --> 00:02:05.976
- [Mark] Right, yeah.

00:02:05.976 --> 00:02:07.550
- That shit's fake on there,

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.620
'cause when you get hit with a chair,

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.470
you feel it, all right?

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.400
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.850
- And dude hit him four
times with a metal chair.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.490
Caved his head in.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.451
- [Mark] Caved his head in?

00:02:16.451 --> 00:02:17.703
- Yeah.

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:18.541
- [Mark] Oof.

00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:20.310
- Shit's crazy.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.143
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.930
So a lot of drugs are going on down here.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.220
Are you worried about any of them?

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.053
- [Matt] Oh, no.

00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:30.503
I don't drink, I don't do
drugs, I don't do none of that.

00:02:32.128 --> 00:02:35.873
I've been sober from
alcohol for three years.

00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:38.100
- [Mark] You drank.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.730
- [Matt] Oh yeah, I drank a lot.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:40.599
- [Mark] So you stopped drinking?

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:41.432
- [Matt] Oh yeah.

00:02:41.432 --> 00:02:42.265
- [Mark] For three years.

00:02:42.265 --> 00:02:43.520
- [Matt] I've not had
a drop in three years.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.353
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:02:44.353 --> 00:02:45.186
- [Matt] Yeah.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.060
I mean, you don't need
to be down here homeless

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.263
and being messed up on dope and alcohol.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.870
'Cause anything could happen to you.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.353
- [Mark] Yeah, no you,
especially as a white guy,

00:02:55.353 --> 00:02:56.953
you're more vulnerable than-

00:02:56.953 --> 00:02:58.203
- [Matt] Oh God, oh yeah.

00:03:01.737 --> 00:03:04.440
- [Mark] What would you like to see happen

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.426
in the next five years for you?

00:03:06.426 --> 00:03:08.423
- [Matt] I'm getting housing again.

00:03:08.423 --> 00:03:11.254
I'm gonna get me another apartment.

00:03:11.254 --> 00:03:14.630
And I'm not gonna have
friends over anymore,

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.980
'cause you see what happened with that,

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.390
I got evicted over them.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.790
So I'm not having no more
friends over my house.

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:27.339
You can't trust people now.

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:28.180
- [Mark] Your family?

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.520
- [Matt] My mom lives in West Virginia,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.070
my dad lives in Oklahoma.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:31.903
- [Mark] Okay.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.520
And you want to go back there,

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.523
you want to stay in California?

00:03:35.523 --> 00:03:37.062
- [Matt] I'm gonna try
and stay in California.

00:03:37.062 --> 00:03:37.895
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:37.895 --> 00:03:38.728
- [Matt] I like the weather here.

00:03:38.728 --> 00:03:39.561
- [Mark] Yeah, the weather's great.

00:03:39.561 --> 00:03:40.477
- [Matt] Yeah.

00:03:40.477 --> 00:03:42.170
Are you from California?

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:43.233
- [Mark] I'm from Chicago originally.

00:03:43.233 --> 00:03:44.066
- [Matt] That's--

00:03:44.066 --> 00:03:45.134
- [Mark] Detroit, Chicago, and then LA.

00:03:45.134 --> 00:03:45.967
- [Matt] It's cold there.

00:03:45.967 --> 00:03:46.800
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:47.660
- [Matt] It's cold there.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.810
- [Mark] Oh yeah, cold.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.243
As a kid what did you dream about?

00:03:54.243 --> 00:03:56.140
When you grew up, what you wanted to be.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:56.973
- A truck driver.

00:03:56.973 --> 00:03:57.959
- [Mark] A truck driver.
- Yeah.

00:03:57.959 --> 00:03:58.860
- [Mark] Have you driven a truck?

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.060
- No.
- [Mark] Never?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.310
- I've been in trucks,
but I never drove one.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.070
- [Mark] You ever been married?

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.020
- No.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.784
- [Mark] No kids?
- No.

00:04:08.784 --> 00:04:09.617
- [Mark] No girlfriend?

00:04:09.617 --> 00:04:10.450
- No.

00:04:11.856 --> 00:04:12.782
- [Mark] Stay out of trouble that way.

00:04:12.782 --> 00:04:13.620
- Oh yeah.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.370
I've not been in trouble since 2000, so...

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:17.984
- [Mark] What trouble did you get in then?

00:04:17.984 --> 00:04:19.180
- Stealin' cars.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.168
- [Mark] Oh you were stealing cars?

00:04:21.168 --> 00:04:22.842
- That was my--
- [Mark] You end up in prison?

00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:24.130
- Oh yeah.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.470
- [Mark] How many years
were you in prison?

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.283
- Last time I was there was, uh,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.013
fourteen months ???

00:04:31.091 --> 00:04:32.170
- [Mark] What state?

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.132
- Oklahoma.

00:04:33.132 --> 00:04:33.965
- [Mark] Oklahoma.

00:04:33.965 --> 00:04:35.671
- Arizona, I was there before that.

00:04:35.671 --> 00:04:37.571
I was there for four and a half years.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.070
I was locked up in
Virginia for four years.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.556
I've been locked up in West Virginia.

00:04:45.556 --> 00:04:46.389
- [Mark] Oh.

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:47.925
- I did a year in Pennsylvania.

00:04:47.925 --> 00:04:48.758
- [Mark] Oh!

00:04:48.758 --> 00:04:49.594
- Yeah.

00:04:49.594 --> 00:04:50.590
(Mark laughs)

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.703
- [Mark] You like cars.

00:04:51.703 --> 00:04:52.536
- Yeah, I like cars.

00:04:52.536 --> 00:04:53.442
- [Mark] You like other people's cars.

00:04:53.442 --> 00:04:54.644
- Yeah.

00:04:54.644 --> 00:04:55.703
I have a thing with
other people's vehicles.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.693
- [Mark] Okay. And how
do you break into it?

00:04:58.693 --> 00:05:00.060
- They were unlocked.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.122
- [Mark] They were unlocked and you just--

00:05:01.122 --> 00:05:02.200
They were unlocked and I just went

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.522
on and got on in 'em.

00:05:03.522 --> 00:05:04.355
- [Mark] Hot wired?

00:05:04.355 --> 00:05:05.692
- Hot wired 'em and I was gone.

00:05:05.692 --> 00:05:07.947
(Mark laughs)

00:05:07.947 --> 00:05:11.373
- You can disconnect the alarm easy.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.493
- [Mark] Yeah, makes it easy to--

00:05:13.493 --> 00:05:15.790
- All you gotta do is raise your hood

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.670
and there's two wires there

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.020
which ones you click is what

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.871
cuts off your alarm, all right?

00:05:19.871 --> 00:05:20.910
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.610
- Yeah. My brother taught me that.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.123
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:05:26.123 --> 00:05:26.956
Well, thank you for talking to me.

00:05:26.956 --> 00:05:28.153
I appreciate the time.

00:05:29.414 --> 00:05:31.331
All right. Thanks, man.

00:05:32.893 --> 00:05:33.763
- [Mark] How many cars have you stolen?

00:05:33.763 --> 00:05:35.568
- I've stolen over a hundred I know.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:36.570
- [Mark] Over a hundred cars?
- Yeah.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.050
- [Mark] At what age did you start?

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:38.883
- 'Bout fourteen.

00:05:38.883 --> 00:05:39.716
- [Mark] Fourteen years old you

00:05:39.716 --> 00:05:40.750
stole your first car?

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:41.583
- Yeah.

00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:42.416
- [Mark] You don't even have a driver's

00:05:42.416 --> 00:05:43.249
license at fourteen.

00:05:43.249 --> 00:05:45.680
- No, I never had a
driver's license in my life.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:46.893
- [Mark] You still don't
have a driver's license?

00:05:46.893 --> 00:05:49.560
- No. I can't get a driver's license.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.393
- [Mark] Why is that?

00:05:50.393 --> 00:05:53.440
- Somebody in Arizona
got ahold of my birth

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.860
certificate and obtained an Arizona

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.560
driver's license, but they don't have no

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.960
record of who they gave it to.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.060
How is that even possible?

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.940
So I couldn't even get an ID in Arizona.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.785
- [Mark] So you don't even have an ID

00:06:07.785 --> 00:06:09.474
to get a driver's license

00:06:09.474 --> 00:06:10.307
in the first place?

00:06:10.307 --> 00:06:13.680
- Well I have an ID here in California.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:14.663
I have an ID.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.073
Arizona wouldn't even let me get an ID.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.090
Arizona is just messed up.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.582
- [Mark] So, tell me about the

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:26.160
Porsche that you stole.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.810
- Well, I went into the hospital,

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.643
because my mom works there.

00:06:28.643 --> 00:06:31.290
I was gonna get some money from her

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.640
to go buy some weed, right?

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.190
I leave the hospital,

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:37.620
doctor rolls right up in this Porsche.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.100
Rolls right up, lefts it runnin'

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.280
and runs in the hospital.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.650
Leaves it runnin'!

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.710
Shit, I jumped in that sum bitch

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:43.833
and I took off!

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:46.410
I took it to North Carolina

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.010
and I got rid of it.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.359
- [Mark] For how much?

00:06:50.359 --> 00:06:51.192
- Five thousand.

00:06:51.192 --> 00:06:52.615
- [Mark] Five thousand
bucks you sold the Porsche?

00:06:52.615 --> 00:06:53.683
- Yep.

00:06:53.683 --> 00:06:56.400
It wasn't mine, I didn't care.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.965
It's probably worth a lot
more than that though.

00:06:57.965 --> 00:07:00.476
- [Mark] What?
- The Porsche.

00:07:00.476 --> 00:07:01.644
- [Mark] That's funny.

00:07:01.644 --> 00:07:02.477
- Uh huh.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:08.910
- [Mark] And is it
exciting stealing a car?

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.183
The adrenaline and all the--

00:07:10.183 --> 00:07:11.016
- Yeah.

00:07:11.016 --> 00:07:11.849
It's definitely a rush.

00:07:11.849 --> 00:07:12.682
- [Mark] It's gotta be exciting, right?

00:07:12.682 --> 00:07:13.821
- It's definitely a rush

00:07:13.821 --> 00:07:16.830
to steal somebody's car.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:17.663
But I never car jacked

00:07:17.663 --> 00:07:18.810
nobody though.
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:19.650
- Never done that.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:20.550
- [Mark] You're stealing cars that have

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.480
nobody in them.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.403
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.957
Car jacking, that's serious time there.

00:07:24.957 --> 00:07:26.260
- [Mark] What's the most money you ever

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:27.545
made selling a car?

00:07:27.545 --> 00:07:28.940
- (mumbles)

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.200
- [Mark] What's that?
- Twelve thousand.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.379
- [Mark] Twelve grand? For what?

00:07:31.379 --> 00:07:32.453
- A Lincoln.
- [Mark] A Lincoln?

00:07:32.453 --> 00:07:33.770
- A brand new Lincoln.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:36.563
- [Mark] And the people you're selling

00:07:36.563 --> 00:07:37.710
them to know that they're hot, right?

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:40.063
- Oh yeah. They take 'em to a chop shop.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:43.033
They know the sum bitches are stolen.

00:07:43.033 --> 00:07:44.266
They don't care.

00:07:44.266 --> 00:07:46.416
All they're gonna do
is chop 'em up anyway.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:48.790
- [Mark] Oh.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.741
Interesting.

00:07:51.741 --> 00:07:52.920
- You ain't ever stole a car?

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.070
- [Mark] I've never stolen a car.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:54.952
- Wow.

00:07:54.952 --> 00:07:55.870
(Mark laughs)

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:56.990
- Have you ever thought about it?

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.100
- [Mark] No, I've never
even thought about it.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.310
Maybe I should.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.760
- No.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.297
They give out serious time
for stealing cars now.

00:08:05.297 --> 00:08:07.370
- [Mark] How many years in jail, prison,

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:08.765
have you done for stealing cars?

00:08:08.765 --> 00:08:09.598
- Eight years.

00:08:09.598 --> 00:08:12.181
- [Mark] Eight years?
- Uh huh.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.482
- [Mark] What's it like in prison?

00:08:15.482 --> 00:08:17.340
What state were you in prison?

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.180
- I've been in prison in
four different states.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.013
- [Mark] Oh really?

00:08:20.013 --> 00:08:22.543
- West Virginia, Virginia,
Arizona, and Oklahoma.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.740
- [Mark] And what's it like?

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.050
- Virginia was really messed up.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.006
- [Mark] Why is that?

00:08:29.006 --> 00:08:31.222
- I was in maximum security prison.

00:08:31.222 --> 00:08:32.967
I ain't had but six years,

00:08:32.967 --> 00:08:34.010
but I'm doin' time with m'fers that

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.420
got three and four life sentences

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.307
they ain't got shit to lose, right?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.270
They threw me there because

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:43.921
when they arrested me for a car, right,

00:08:43.921 --> 00:08:48.550
it was a truck I stole in Virginia, right,

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.970
underneath the seat was a 357 magnum.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:51.803
- [Mark] Oh no.

00:08:51.803 --> 00:08:52.960
- And they charged me with it.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:54.620
It was in the vehicle I stole though.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.620
I didn't know the damn thing was in there.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.350
I got charged with it.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.880
A weapons charge.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.100
I'd aggravated it,

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.470
so they aggravated my sentence

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.660
and sent me to a maximum security prison.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.150
- [Mark] Oh shit.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.360
- Ended up maxin' that number out.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.210
I did, uh, three and a half on a six.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.310
- [Mark] Wow.
- Yeah.

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:16.791
And Virginia wasn't nothin' nice.

00:09:16.791 --> 00:09:19.950
They had a riot when I was there,

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:20.783
they killed guards,

00:09:20.783 --> 00:09:22.090
they killed inmates,

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.340
they burned down the kitchen,

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.980
they burned down the commissary.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:25.813
- [Mark] Really?

00:09:25.813 --> 00:09:27.000
- They just wrecked the whole yard.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.160
- [Mark] Which prison?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.595
- That was the maximum security prison,

00:09:29.595 --> 00:09:31.110
South Hampton.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:31.943
- [Mark] Wow.

00:09:31.943 --> 00:09:33.090
- That was a rough place.

00:09:35.226 --> 00:09:38.134
There was no joking there.

00:09:38.134 --> 00:09:41.403
I seen people get stabbed, beat up.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:45.225
- [Mark] How do you steer
clear of all that stuff?

00:09:45.225 --> 00:09:47.689
- The best thing to do, is you know

00:09:47.689 --> 00:09:49.520
not to do in prison...

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.810
You don't mess with dope.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:51.643
- [Mark] You don't mess with dope.

00:09:51.643 --> 00:09:52.850
- If you can't pay for it.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.200
You don't gamble.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.580
You don't mess with homosexuals.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:57.880
A lot of people be doin' that.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.380
They messin' with them homosexuals

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.191
and they caught up in shit.

00:10:01.191 --> 00:10:03.220
You don't do that.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:04.370
- [Mark] There's no women around.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.960
- These people in prison that are

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:07.910
dressed up like women,

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:10.669
they think they are women, all right?

00:10:10.669 --> 00:10:11.502
- [Mark] Really?

00:10:11.502 --> 00:10:14.063
Yeah, they want you to
address them as ma'am.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:15.923
You know.

00:10:15.923 --> 00:10:18.127
As female things, you
know what I'm sayin'?

00:10:18.127 --> 00:10:18.960
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.613
- They don't wanna be called men, no.

00:10:21.613 --> 00:10:25.333
They wanna be considered females in there.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:31.050
I seen it all in there though.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:33.773
In Virginia I seen
everything happen in there.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:35.940
But then, ya know, you been

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:36.800
down to Skid Row.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.396
You seen all kinds of
crazy shit down there.

00:10:38.396 --> 00:10:39.229
- [Mark] Oh yeah.

00:10:39.229 --> 00:10:40.920
- You seen your little table set up.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:43.900
Selling their little meth pipes.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:45.070
- [Mark] Yeah, seen it all.
- Aw man.

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:45.910
- [Mark] Right there in the street.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:46.743
- They don't care.

00:10:46.743 --> 00:10:47.640
- [Mark] The cops walk right by.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:48.890
- They don't give a fuck.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.123
They got bigger fish to fry, I guess.

00:10:52.123 --> 00:10:53.540
- [Mark] I guess.

00:10:54.552 --> 00:10:55.385
- I never been messed with

00:10:55.385 --> 00:10:57.853
by the police here though.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.851
- [Mark] Well you don't look like trouble.

00:10:59.851 --> 00:11:02.247
- Well, you're allowed to panhandle here.

00:11:02.247 --> 00:11:03.080
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.583
So you're just a homeless guy panhandling?

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:09.670
You're not a threat like,
maybe some of the...

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:12.000
- Nah, I'm not out there
trying to get money

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:12.980
for dope and shit.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:13.813
- [Mark] Yeah, yeah.

00:11:13.813 --> 00:11:15.070
- Robbin' people and shit, no.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.840
That goes on a lot here.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:18.673
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:11:18.673 --> 00:11:20.431
- That goes on a lot here in Skid Row,

00:11:20.431 --> 00:11:21.528
a lot of robbery.

00:11:21.528 --> 00:11:22.361
- [Mark] A lot of robbery?

00:11:22.361 --> 00:11:23.244
- Oh yeah. -
[Mark] Oh yeah.

00:11:23.244 --> 00:11:24.232
- They have stuff sittin' out and

00:11:24.232 --> 00:11:26.514
m'fers walk by and snatch it, aight?

00:11:26.514 --> 00:11:27.597
- [Mark] Oh yeah.

00:11:27.597 --> 00:11:28.430
(gasps)

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.750
- [Mark] You walk away from your tent,

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.541
with anything valuable inside that tent.

00:11:31.541 --> 00:11:32.374
(laughs)

00:11:32.374 --> 00:11:33.403
Good luck.

00:11:33.403 --> 00:11:34.630
I mean, I think what they do

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:35.630
is they get people high,

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.090
they give them some spice or whatever,

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.240
they get high, they pass out,

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:39.340
and then they rob 'em.

00:11:41.922 --> 00:11:42.755
- [Mark] All right, man.

00:11:42.755 --> 00:11:43.879
Well thank you for talking to me again.

00:11:43.879 --> 00:11:44.712
Really interesting.

00:11:44.712 --> 00:11:47.427
You got a lot of interesting stories.

00:11:47.427 --> 00:11:49.290
You gonna steal any cars this year?

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:50.470
- No sir.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:51.303
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:11:51.303 --> 00:11:52.150
- I don't do nothin' wrong now.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.317
I'm law and order.

00:11:53.317 --> 00:11:54.150
- [Mark] Is that right?

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.696
- I don't do nothin' wrong.

00:11:55.696 --> 00:11:57.280
I do not break the law at all.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.593
- [Mark] But you're smoking spice?

00:11:58.593 --> 00:11:59.824
- That's legal.

00:11:59.824 --> 00:12:01.424
- [Mark] Ah, it's legal.

00:12:01.424 --> 00:12:02.382
- Yeah.

00:12:02.382 --> 00:12:04.030
- [Mark] I don't think
it's good for you though.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.863
- Well--

00:12:04.863 --> 00:12:07.254
- [Mark] I don't, just be
careful with that shit.

00:12:07.254 --> 00:12:09.080
- It's better than doin' meth I guess.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.130
- [Mark] I don't know.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:10.963
It's all bad.

00:12:10.963 --> 00:12:12.069
- It's all bad.

00:12:12.069 --> 00:12:12.902
(Mark laughs)

00:12:12.902 --> 00:12:14.130
- Cocaine, meth, it's all bad.

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:18.820
Man, but what do ya do, huh?

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.060
- [Mark] Well you gotta pass

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.930
the time somehow, right?

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:23.180
It's good to stay busy.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.170
- [Matt] Just keep away
from certain things.

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:27.018
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:12:27.018 --> 00:12:28.770
Stay away from this neighborhood.

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:29.768
Stay busy.

00:12:29.768 --> 00:12:30.601
- Fuckin' neighborhood.

00:12:30.601 --> 00:12:32.394
- [Mark] Push the boulder up hill.

00:12:32.394 --> 00:12:33.927
That's all you can do.

00:12:33.927 --> 00:12:34.890
All right, man.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.103
Thanks for talking to me!

